  "rationale": "The spec requires max_abs_err <= 2^-20 and throughput >= 50 MSPS, with selection by min luts_plus_ffs. The error constraint requires sufficient n_iter and data_width; the throughput constraint requires either pipelined/pipelined_m (1 result/cycle) or very high Fmax for iterative. Pipelined_m is likely the best area/throughput trade-off since it reduces FF count vs fully pipelined while maintaining 1 result/cycle. We allocate 40% to pipelined, 35% to pipelined_m, and 15% to iterative (to confirm infeasibility). We search n_iter 20-30 and data_width 22-28 to find the minimal-area designs that meet the 2^-20 error bound. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small (0-2) to minimize area while still meeting error. Rounding is explored for both trunc and round to see if rounding helps meet the error bound with fewer iterations."
}

